<h3><strong><img decoding="async" class="size-medium wp-image-9040 alignright" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20300%20200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="" width="300" height="200" data-lazy-srcset="https://mochf.[long].jpg 300w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1024w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 768w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1536w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 2048w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1120w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1350w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" data-lazy-src="https://mochf.[long].jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" class="size-medium wp-image-9040 alignright" src="https://mochf.[long].jpg" alt="" width="300" height="200" srcset="https://mochf.[long].jpg 300w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1024w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 768w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1536w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 2048w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1120w, https://mochf.[long].jpg 1350w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></noscript>About MoNASP Scholarships </strong></h3>
<p>The Missouri Conservation Heritage Foundation (MCHF) is proud to award $30,000 in scholarships each year to the top five male and female archers in both bullseye and 3D at the MoNASP State Archery Championship. These scholarships are made possible through the Chip and Teresa McGeehan Archery in the Schools Conservation Fund, the Daniel Duncan Archery in the Schools Scholarship Fund, MCHF and a matching grant from the National Archery in the Schools Program (NASP). These scholarships are awarded to students for their education endeavors after graduation.</p>
<p>Scholarship funds are released to the winners after graduation from high school and once proof of enrollment in a university, community college, technical college or trade school has been provided. MCHF will hold scholarship funds on the student’s behalf until eligibility is met.</p>
